    {
      "id": "FZR-01",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-flag-regulator-cover",
      "title": "Small ideals cover the unit torus and bound the class number times the regulator",
      "statement": "For a totally complex number field of degree 2f with Y the square root of its absolute discriminant, hR ≤ Y^s(s/(s−1))^(2f) for every real s>1. In any fixed ideal class the regulator is at most the sum over nonzero integral ideals of norm ≤Y of log(Y/N𝔞)^(f−1)/(f−1)!.",
      "hypotheses": "Integral ideal classes in the maximal order, ordinary Euclidean measure at each complex place, weighted logarithms twice the log modulus, and regulator measured after one coordinate is deleted. The rank-zero simplex has volume one.",
      "correspondence": "The proof derives the covering of the unit torus using the same inverse ideal class, Minkowski polydisc, and dimensions as the source. The final Euler-product comparison provides the same upper bound as the source’s finite counts of ideals of given norm.",
      "dependencies": [
        "CLM-01"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "global-flag-class-regulator-bound"
      ],
