    {
      "id": "FZR-02",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-flag-zeta-residue",
      "title": "The residue at one and its cost in a prescribed flag type",
      "statement": "For every totally complex E of degree 2f and root discriminant d, 0<Res₁ ζ_E≤(16 log d)^(2f). For a positive rank-jump profile of length a and total rank J in ambient rank n, log d≤exp n gives (Res₁ ζ_E)^a≤exp(2fJ(3+n)).",
      "hypotheses": "The field bound uses the analytic class number formula with torsion order w, the lower bound d≥3/2 and the class-number regulator estimate. Applying it to the displayed flag coefficient uses the CM data of the finite-unramified flag-volume branch. Positive jumps imply a≤J.",
      "correspondence": "The numerical comparison takes s=1+1/log d. A short application of the classical ideal-class Minkowski bound supplies the source’s d≥3/2 premise. The consumer invokes this residue estimate separately from its bound on ordinary zeta values at integer arguments at least two. The example only uses the totally complex field theorem. The elementary logarithmic majorant and telescoping geometric series in the exposition prove the same bound exp(2f) for one block of ordinary values.",
      "dependencies": [
        "FZR-01",
        "CLM-01",
        "CLM-05"
      ],
